 Implementing Idempotence in Ansible
Objectives
Design and validate Ansible playbooks that produce zero changes on repeated execution against an already-converged system
Identify structural patterns that break idempotence (unbounded shell appends, timestamp-keyed side effects, unconditional restarts) and replace them with declarative equivalents
Build a self-contained verification harness that quantifies changed-task counts across multiple runs and fails if convergence is not achieved by the second run
Prerequisites
Comfort navigating and editing files on a Linux command line, including file permissions and ownership concepts
Familiarity with YAML syntax and the difference between declarative and imperative configuration
Understanding of Linux service management concepts (start, stop, enable, reload) and what a systemd unit file contains
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

